pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi)

The per-provider request differences in src/providers/presets.ts and
src/providers/openai.ts (which token-limit field a provider accepts, how each
provider switches reasoning on, and DeepSeek's reasoning replay) follow the
provider compatibility behaviour of pi's AI package. The ChatGPT and
OpenRouter sign-in sequences in src/auth/vendors/ (the request parameters each
vendor expects and the checks on its answer) follow the sign-in behaviour of
the same package. So do the xAI, Kimi and Meta device sign-in sequences in
src/auth/vendors-unofficial/ (the request parameters, the words each vendor
answers with, Meta's exchange of an identity token for a key, and when a
refused renewal means signing in again). Runrail does not depend on pi and
ships none of its files.
